      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. The original has a lot of dead code (unused methods, an invalid generic method signature with `T`, unused imports). I'll write a clean, understandable version that keeps only what's needed.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes all dead code (unused helper methods, the invalid generic `T` method signature, and unused imports), retains only the two setup methods and the single test method, and adds inline comments that explain the 72-bit → 2-longs requirement, the meaning of `2L`, and why the merge of a \"short\" extractor is expected to succeed with cardinality 1."
